# Poway Woman's Club — API (Backend)

The **backend API** for the Poway Woman's Club website. A
[Flask](https://flask.palletsprojects.com/) application that handles
authentication, events and RSVPs, the club blog, groups, member profiles,
messaging, and payments.

The [frontend](https://github.com/Poway-Women-s-Club/pwc) (a Jekyll site on
GitHub Pages) calls this API for all of its interactive features.

- **Backend (this repo):** [`Poway-Women-s-Club/pwc-flask`](https://github.com/Poway-Women-s-Club/pwc-flask)
- **Frontend:** [`Poway-Women-s-Club/pwc`](https://github.com/Poway-Women-s-Club/pwc)

---

## Tech stack

- **Flask 3** with an application-factory pattern (`create_app` in `app.py`)
- **Flask-SQLAlchemy** for the database (SQLite by default; PostgreSQL supported)
- **Flask-Login** for session-based authentication
- **Flask-CORS** for cross-origin requests from the GitHub Pages frontend
- **APScheduler** for background event-reminder jobs
- **Pillow** for avatar image handling
- Google OAuth and SMTP email (both optional)
- **Docker** support for deployment

---

## Project structure

```
pwc-flask/
├── app.py               Application factory: config, extensions, blueprints, seeding
├── main.py               Entry point — runs the app on port 8327
├── api/                  Route blueprints
│   ├── auth.py            Register / login / logout / Google OAuth
│   ├── events.py          Events, RSVPs, public RSVPs, meeting requests
│   ├── blog.py            Posts, comments, pinning
│   ├── groups.py          Groups and group applications
│   ├── messages.py        Member-to-member messaging
│   ├── friends.py         Friend requests and connections
│   ├── profile.py         Profiles, avatars, recommendations
│   ├── payments.py        Membership dues (stub) and history
│   ├── admin.py           Admin dashboard, user management
│   └── reminder_jobs.py   Background event-reminder logic
├── model/                SQLAlchemy models (User, Event, BlogPost, Group, …)
├── services/             Email and recommendation helpers
├── templates/            Server-rendered admin page
├── instance/             SQLite database + uploaded avatars (created at runtime)
├── Dockerfile            Production image (gunicorn)
└── docker-compose.yml    Container orchestration
```

---

## Running locally

You need **Python 3.11+**.

```bash
# 1. Create and activate a virtual environment
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate

# 2. Install dependencies
pip install -r requirements.txt

# 3. Create your environment file
cp .env.example .env       # then edit it with your values

# 4. Run the API (http://localhost:8327)
python main.py
```

On first run, the app creates the database and seeds a default admin account:

- **username:** `admin`
- **password:** `admin`

**Change this password immediately** after first login.

---

## Configuration

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in the values you need. Key settings:

| Variable | Purpose |
|----------|---------|
| `SECRET_KEY` | Flask session signing key. Set a real value in production. |
| `DATABASE_URL` | Database connection string. Defaults to SQLite. |
| `GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` / `GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET` | Google OAuth (optional — leave blank to disable). |
| `FRONTEND_URL` / `CORS_EXTRA_ORIGINS` | Allowed origins for CORS and OAuth redirects. |
| `PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | Public URL of this API, used for absolute avatar links. |
| `SESSION_COOKIE_CROSS_SITE` | Set to `1` when frontend and API are on different HTTPS domains. |
| `MAIL_*` | SMTP settings for event-reminder emails (optional). |

> **Local vs. deployed cookies:** On plain `http://localhost`, leave
> `SESSION_COOKIE_CROSS_SITE` unset. When the frontend (GitHub Pages, HTTPS) and
> this API are on different HTTPS hosts, set `SESSION_COOKIE_CROSS_SITE=1` so
> browsers send session cookies on API calls.

---

## API overview

All routes are prefixed with `/api`. A health check is available at
`/api/health` (returns `{"status":"ok"}`).

| Blueprint | Prefix | Handles |
|-----------|--------|---------|
| Auth | `/api/auth` | Register, login, logout, current user, Google OAuth |
| Events | `/api/events` | Events, RSVPs, public RSVPs, meeting requests, attendee counts |
| Blog | `/api/blog` | Posts, comments, pinning |
| Groups | `/api/groups` | Groups, membership, join applications |
| Messages | `/api/messages` | Conversations and unread counts |
| Friends | `/api/friends` | Friend requests, status, search |
| Profile | `/api/profile` | Profiles, avatars, password changes, recommendations |
| Payments | `/api/payments` | Membership dues and payment history |
| Admin | `/api/admin` | Dashboard stats and user management |

### Selected endpoints

**Auth (`/api/auth`)**

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| POST | `/register` | No | `{username, email, password}` |
| POST | `/login` | No | `{username, password}` (username or email) |
| POST | `/logout` | Yes | End the session |
| GET | `/me` | Yes | Return the current user |
| POST | `/google` | No | Google OAuth sign-in |

**Events (`/api/events`)**

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/` | No | List events |
| GET | `/<id>` | No | Single event |
| POST | `/` | Admin | Create an event |
| PUT/DELETE | `/<id>` | Admin | Update or delete an event |
| POST/DELETE | `/<id>/rsvp` | Yes | RSVP or cancel RSVP |
| POST | `/public-rsvp` | No | RSVP as a non-member visitor |
| POST | `/meeting-request` | No | Request a meeting |

**Blog (`/api/blog`)**

| Method | Path | Auth | Description |
|--------|------|------|-------------|
| GET | `/posts` | No | List posts |
| GET | `/posts/<id>` | No | Single post with comments |
| POST | `/posts` | Yes | Create a post |
| PUT/DELETE | `/posts/<id>` | Author/Admin | Update or delete a post |
| POST/DELETE | `/posts/<id>/pin` | Officer/Admin | Pin or unpin a post |
| POST | `/posts/<id>/comments` | Yes | Add a comment |

See the blueprint files in `api/` for the full route list.

---

## Deployment with Docker

```bash
docker compose up --build
```

This builds the image and runs the API on port `8327` using gunicorn. The
`instance/` directory is mounted as a volume so the database and uploaded
avatars persist across restarts. A sample nginx reverse-proxy config is
included in `nginx_file` and `deploy/`.

For production, uncomment `gunicorn` and `psycopg2-binary` in
`requirements.txt` if you plan to use PostgreSQL instead of SQLite.

---

## Security notes

- Change the seeded `admin` / `admin` account password immediately.
- Set a strong `SECRET_KEY` in production — never use the default.
- Keep `.env` out of version control (it is in `.gitignore`).

